# cisco_ios.magic — Cisco IOS firmware identification signatures
#
# Identifies Cisco IOS firmware images at the blob level (before any extraction).
# Covers: IOS monolithic images (outer self-extracting wrapper + inner C*-UN.BIN),
#         IOS-XE packages, and legacy IOS .bin files.
#
# Key discriminator: ELF e_machine = 0x00C0 (192, "CloudShield") — Cisco's custom
# machine type for MIPS32-BE IOS images on ISR/ASR platforms.
#
# Install: cp cisco_ios.magic ~/.local/share/radare2/magic/
# Usage:   file -m cisco_ios.magic <blob>
#          /m ~/.local/share/radare2/magic/cisco_ios.magic    (from r2)
#
# Tested on: 15 x c1900-universalk9-mz.SPA images (15.0(1)M through 15.2(1)T)

# =============================================================================
# Cisco IOS Monolithic ELF (wrapper and inner binary)
#
# Discriminator chain:
#   offset 0:  7F 45 4C 46  (ELF magic)
#   offset 4:  01           (32-bit)
#   offset 5:  02           (big-endian)
#   offset 18: 00 C0        (e_machine = 0xC0 = Cisco IOS)
#   offset 24: entry = 0x81000000 (KSEG0 base)
#
# Two sub-types:
#   Wrapper (self-extracting): e_flags = 0x20002001, 8 section headers, ZIP payload
#   Inner (C*-UN.BIN):         e_flags = 0x10001001, 11 section headers, actual IOS
# =============================================================================

# Match: ELF 32-bit MSB with e_machine=0x00C0 (C1900/C2900/C3900 — MIPS32-BE)
0	string		\x7fELF		
>4	byte		1		
>>5	byte		2		
>>>18	beshort		0x00C0		Cisco IOS ELF image (e_machine=0xC0, MIPS32-BE)

# Match: ELF 32-bit MSB with e_machine=0x0033 (C1700 — PPC32-BE)
# NOTE: readelf/file call this "Stanford MIPS-X" but the ISA is actually PowerPC!
0	string		\x7fELF		
>4	byte		1		
>>5	byte		2		
>>>18	beshort		0x0033		Cisco IOS ELF image (e_machine=0x33 Stanford_MIPS-X=PPC32-BE, c1700)
>>>>36	belong		0x10001001	\b, inner IOS binary (e_flags=0x10001001)
>>>>>48	beshort		11		\b, 11 sections (C*-UN.BIN monolithic image)
>>>>>48	beshort		!11		\b, %d sections
>>>>36	belong		0x20002001	\b, self-extracting wrapper (e_flags=0x20002001)
>>>>>48	beshort		8		\b, 8 sections (ZIP payload embedded)
>>>>36	belong		!0x10001001
>>>>>36	belong		!0x20002001	\b, e_flags=0x%08x (unknown variant)
>>>>24	belong		0x81000000	\b, entry=0x81000000 (KSEG0)
>>>>24	belong		!0x81000000	\b, entry=0x%08x

# =============================================================================
# Cisco IOS ZIP payload inside wrapper
#
# The wrapper contains an embedded ZIP with filename "C*-UN.BIN" at a
# variable offset (~94K-104K depending on version). We match the ZIP
# local file header + filename pattern.
# =============================================================================

# ZIP local file header 50 4B 03 04 with IOS filename pattern
0	string		PK\x03\x04	
>26	beshort		>8		
>>30	string		C1900-UN.BIN	Cisco IOS 1900 Series payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)
>>30	string		C2900-UN.BIN	Cisco IOS 2900 Series payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)
>>30	string		C3900-UN.BIN	Cisco IOS 3900 Series payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)
>>30	string		C800-UN.BIN	Cisco IOS 800 Series payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)
>>30	string		C1800-UN.BIN	Cisco IOS 1800 Series payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)
>>30	string		C7200-UN.BIN	Cisco IOS 7200 Series payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)
>>30	string		C1700-TP.BIN	Cisco IOS 1700 Series PAGENT payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)
>>30	string		C1700-AD.BIN	Cisco IOS 1700 Series AdventEnterprise payload
>>30	regex		C1700-.*\.BIN	Cisco IOS 1700 Series payload (extracted from wrapper ZIP)

# =============================================================================
# Cisco IOS version identification strings
#
# CW_SYSDESCR is the canonical version identifier, always present in IOS images.
# Format: CW_SYSDESCR$Cisco IOS Software, <platform> Software (<image>), Version <ver>
# =============================================================================

0	search/4096	CW_SYSDESCR$Cisco IOS	Cisco IOS version descriptor
>0	string		x	\b: %.80s

# Also match in rodata region of large binaries (search deeper)
0	search/131072	Cisco IOS Software,	Cisco IOS Software identification string
>0	string		x	\b: %.100s

# =============================================================================
# Cisco IOS-XE / Bundle Mode
#
# IOS-XE uses a different container format (sub-packages in tar/gzip)
# Magic: "IOS-XE Software" in version string area
# =============================================================================

0	search/4096	CW_SYSDESCR$Cisco IOS-XE	Cisco IOS-XE version descriptor
>0	string		x	\b: %.80s

# =============================================================================
# Cisco ROMMON (ROM Monitor)
#
# ROMMON has a different signature — smaller binary, different entry
# Magic: "ROMMON" string near start
# =============================================================================

0	search/1024	ROMMON		
>0	string		x		Cisco ROMMON image marker: %.20s

# =============================================================================
# Cisco IOS copyright string (present in all IOS images)
#
# This is a fallback matcher for fragments or partial images
# =============================================================================

0	search/131072	Copyright (c) 1986	
>0	regex		Cisco Systems	Cisco IOS copyright (1986-era, Cisco Systems)

# =============================================================================
# Cisco IOS c1700 self-decompressing wrapper (FEEDFACE + PKZIP)
#
# c1700 -mz images use a different container than C1900:
#   e_machine = 0x33 (Stanford MIPS-X → actually PPC)
#   Entry: 0x80008000
#   Section [6] at file offset ~0x467c contains:
#     FEEDFACE magic (4 bytes) + sizes/checksums + PK\x03\x04 ZIP container
#   The ZIP contains a single file: C1700-XX.BIN (the decompressed IOS)
#
# Match FEEDFACE followed by PKZIP within 32 bytes
# =============================================================================

0	belong		0xFEEDFACE	
>20	string		PK\x03\x04	Cisco IOS c1700 FEEDFACE+PKZIP compressed payload
>>50	string		x		\b, inner file: %.20s

